**2. Wire it up in `Program.cs`:**

```csharp
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();
builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<CustomExceptionHandler>();

var app = builder.Build();

app.UseExceptionHandler();   // must be before routing

// your endpoints here
app.MapGet("/example/{id}", (int id) =>
{
    throw new KeyNotFoundException($"Item {id} not found");
});

app.Run();
```

**How it works:**

| Component | Role |
|-----------|------|
| `AddProblemDetails()` | Configures RFC 7807 content type (`application/problem+json`) |
| `AddExceptionHandler<T>()` | Registers your custom handler in DI |
| `UseExceptionHandler()` | Catches exceptions globally — no per-endpoint try/catch needed |
| `IExceptionHandler` | Your mapping logic runs for every unhandled exception |

**Example response** (404):
```json
{
  "status": 404,
  "title": "Resource not found",
  "detail": "Item 42 not found"
}
```

For 500s, `Detail` is intentionally `null` so stack traces and internal messages never leak to clients. If you want to log those, inject `ILogger<CustomExceptionHandler>` and log before returning.
